### 🔑 Key AI Use Cases in CI/CD

#### A. AI-Generated GitHub Actions YAML

**🟠 GitHub Actions ಯಾಮ್ಲ್ ರಚನೆ:** GitHub Copilot ಸ್ವಯಂಚಾಲಿತವಾಗಿ YAML ಪೈಪ್‌ಲೈನ್ ಫೈಲ್‌ಗಳನ್ನು ರಚಿಸಬಹುದು.

```yaml
# AI-Generated example (GitHub Copilot prompt:
# "Create a CI workflow for a Python app with AI-powered test selection")

name: AI-Assisted CI Pipeline
on: [push, pull_request]

jobs:
  ai-code-review:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: AI Code Quality Gate
        uses: github/super-linter@v5
        env:
          GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}

      - name: AI-Powered Test Selection
        run: |
          # Use AI to identify which tests are impacted by this change
          python ai_test_selector.py --diff ${{ github.sha }}

      - name: Run Selected Tests
        run: pytest tests/ --markers="ai_selected"

      - name: AI Security Scan
        uses: github/codeql-action/analyze@v3

  deploy-with-ai-rollback:
    needs: ai-code-review
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - name: Deploy
        run: ./deploy.sh

      - name: AI Anomaly Monitor (Post-Deploy)
        run: |
          python monitor.py --mode=ai --threshold=0.95 --window=5m
```

#### B. Flaky Test Prediction

```
ಫ್ಲೇಕಿ ಟೆಸ್ಟ್ ಭವಿಷ್ಯವಾಣಿ (Flaky Test Prediction):

  Historical Test Data ──► ML Model ──► Flakiness Score
        │                                      │
        │ (pass/fail patterns,                  │ 0.0 = Stable
        │  timing, env variables)               │ 1.0 = Very Flaky
        │                                       ▼
        └──────────────────────────────── Quarantine
                                          Flaky Tests
                                          Before CI Run
```

### 🎯 Interview Questions — CI/CD

**Q1:** *"How would you integrate AI into a GitHub Actions pipeline without introducing security risks?"*

```
💡 Answer Framework:
  ✅ Use AI for: code review scoring, test selection, anomaly detection
  ✅ Keep secrets in: GitHub Secrets, never in AI prompts
  ✅ Add a human gate: AI suggestions → human approval → merge
  ✅ Audit AI outputs: log all AI-generated YAML changes
  ❌ Avoid: AI directly pushing to main without review
  ❌ Avoid: Sending production secrets to external LLM APIs
```

**Q2:** *"Describe a scenario where AI made your CI/CD pipeline worse."*

```
💡 Story Template:
  SITUATION: AI-generated tests had 30% false positives
  TASK: Needed to reduce noise without losing coverage
  ACTION: Added confidence threshold filter + human review queue
  RESULT: False positive rate dropped to 4%, team trust restored
```

