### AI-Assisted Dockerfile (Example)

```dockerfile
# ================================
# Stage 1: Builder (AI-generated multi-stage)
# Prompt used: "Optimize this Dockerfile for a FastAPI ML inference app"
# ================================
FROM python:3.11-slim AS builder

WORKDIR /build

# AI TIP: Cache dependencies before copying source code
COPY requirements.txt .
RUN pip install --no-cache-dir --user -r requirements.txt

# ================================
# Stage 2: Runtime (minimal attack surface)
# AI selected: distroless for security, slim for compatibility
# ================================
FROM python:3.11-slim AS runtime

# AI TIP: Never run as root in production containers
RUN useradd --create-home --shell /bin/bash appuser
WORKDIR /home/appuser/app

# Copy only what's needed (AI identified these paths)
COPY --from=builder /root/.local /home/appuser/.local
COPY ./src ./src
COPY ./models ./models

USER appuser

# AI-suggested health check
HEALTHCHECK --interval=30s --timeout=10s --start-period=5s \
  CMD python -c "import requests; requests.get('http://localhost:8000/health')"

EXPOSE 8000
CMD ["python", "-m", "uvicorn", "src.main:app", "--host", "0.0.0.0"]
```

### 🎯 Interview Questions — Docker

**Q3:** *"How does AI help reduce Docker image size and why does it matter in DevOps?"*

```
💡 Answer Points:
  1. AI analyzes Dockerfile and identifies: unused layers, missing
     .dockerignore, oversized base images
  2. Multi-stage builds (AI-generated) can reduce size 60-80%
  3. Smaller images = faster CI builds, faster deployments, lower
     registry storage costs, smaller attack surface
  4. Tools: GitHub Copilot in editor + Snyk/Trivy in pipeline
```

**Q4:** *"What security risks come with using AI to generate Dockerfiles?"*

```
💡 Answer Points:
  ✅ Risk: AI might suggest FROM ubuntu:latest (no pinned version)
  ✅ Risk: AI might miss COPY permissions, exposing sensitive files
  ✅ Risk: AI-generated RUN commands might skip signature verification
  ✅ Mitigation: Always run AI output through Hadolint + Trivy
  ✅ Mitigation: Pin all base image digests (sha256)
  ✅ Mitigation: Code review gate — no AI Dockerfile goes unchecked
```

