### 🎯 Interview Questions — GitHub Copilot

**Q7:** *"How do you ensure code quality when using GitHub Copilot in a DevOps pipeline?"*

```
💡 Answer Framework (5-point governance model):
  1. ACCEPT POLICY: Only accept suggestions you understand fully
  2. REVIEW GATE: All Copilot-assisted PRs flagged for extra review
  3. TESTING: Copilot code must have same test coverage as human code
  4. SECURITY: Run CodeQL + Dependabot on all Copilot-generated code
  5. AUDIT LOG: Track Copilot usage per engineer for compliance
```

**Q8:** *"What are the limitations of GitHub Copilot for infrastructure code?"*

```
💡 Answer Points:
  ✅ Copilot doesn't know your cloud account structure/naming
  ✅ Copilot may suggest deprecated provider versions
  ✅ Copilot cannot access your real infrastructure state
  ✅ Copilot may miss org-specific security policies
  ✅ Copilot suggestions can have subtle logic errors in loops/conditions
  ✅ Best practice: Use Copilot for boilerplate, human for architecture
```

